    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d821">

                <pb facs="1186" n="1054" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg1054"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.74/672: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacVeagh</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-04-07T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 7, 1926—4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>28. Page 4 of your despatch number 73, March 13, 1926.<anchor n="52"
                        xml:id="d821-f1"/> Department prefers, in view of status of Federal wireless
                    contract in Peking at present, that discussions of the question should not at
                    the present time be initiated at Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
